Fixed. The bug was on line 43 of `src/sim.ts`:

```ts
if (foodSurplus >= 0) {  // before
if (foodSurplus > 0) {   // after
```

`>= 0` treated a zero surplus (production equals consumption) as a growth condition, so population grew even when the settlement was just breaking even on food. Changed to `> 0` so population only grows when there's an actual surplus.

All 4 tests pass.


